# MediaTek SCP sensor hub (sensors behind the SCP)
#

config MTK_SCP_SENSORS
	tristate "Mediatek SCP sensor hub"
	depends on IIO
	depends on MTK_SCP_CM4 || COMPILE_TEST
	help
	  Say y (or M) here to use the motion and environment sensors that are
	  attached to MediaTek's System Companion Processor instead of the AP:
	  on the MT6785 that is the accelerometer, the gyroscope, the
	  magnetometer, the ambient light sensors and the proximity sensor.
	  The SCP firmware drives the parts and this driver brings their data
	  out through /dev/hf_manager and as IIO devices.

	  It needs the SCP driver (MTK_SCP_CM4) to have loaded the firmware.

	  To compile this driver as a module, choose M here: the module is
	  called mtk-scp-sensors.
